course: dictionary
lesson: 2580
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and demonstrate is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it. «Ollie demonstrated a combo on the sofa and his little sister got an elbow in the eye, which was purple for a week.» A combo is a set of moves, so Ollie was showing his moves to someone. Here demonstrate means show how to do something.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Ollie showed a combo on the sofa» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Always ask: what is happening here, and what would fit?
explain: The word can also mean prove. «Demonstrate that 12 is even» means show clearly, with reasons, that it is true. The word can even mean march. «Crowds demonstrated in the streets» means people walked together in public to show support for something, or to protest against it.
fact: Demonstrate can mean show how something works or how to do something.
fact: Demonstrate can mean prove clearly that something is true.
fact: Demonstrate can mean show a feeling or quality by what you do.
fact: Demonstrate can mean march or gather in public to show you support something or are against it.
fact: The forms are demonstrate, demonstrates, demonstrated and demonstrating.
exercise: «Ollie demonstrated a combo on the sofa.» What does demonstrated mean here? | Felt sad about the sofa | Proved that the sofa was strong | *Showed how to do a set of moves | Marched across the room
exercise: Mr Patel says, «Demonstrate that 12 is even.» What must you do? | March around the classroom | Draw a sad face | *Prove clearly that 12 is even | Shout out the answer
exercise: «The crowd demonstrated against the new road.» What does demonstrated mean? | Showed how to build a road | Showed a happy feeling | Proved the road was safe | *Marched together in public to show they were against it
test: «Tara demonstrated great kindness when she shared her lunch.» What quality does this show? | Anger, shown by shouting | Tiredness after a long day | Speed in running | *Kindness, shown by what she did
test: Which form of demonstrate shows that something happened in the past? | demonstrating | demonstrate | *demonstrated | demonstrates
exam: «Demonstrate your answer with a diagram.» What does demonstrate mean in this exam question? | March to the front of the hall | Feel very sad about the question | *Show clearly, so that the answer is proved | Rub the answer out
